  "notes": "Synthetic. Truth is what each line does at run time, except where a policy turns a value into a gap. agent.py:13 reports the __init__ default with a parameter_overridden gap because the constructor call passes o1-mini; agent.py:24 is public, so its client default and the constructor call's gateway are both possible; agent.py:35 is built without the argument. escapes.py:13, :21, :28 and :40 report their default with an unseen_callers gap (the function is passed to an executor, partially applied, mapped or decorated); escapes.py:47 keeps the client default's routing with an unseen_callers gap, :54 with a parameter_default gap (public), and _private_client at :58 has none. bindings.py:47 is globals()[\"MODEL7\"] = \"o3-mini\" at module level, which is MODEL7 = \"o3-mini\": the value is right; bindings.py:55 may be rebound by tune() at any time. overrides.py:10 is assigned after the wildcard import, so it resolves; overrides.py:8 is written before it. subclass.py:27 is a class with no subclass in the file; dicts.py:41 is only read through its aliases. Gap values (the models a run-time choice may give) and values_complete are not compared here; the unit tests check them. credentials.py lists no credential-shaped value anywhere: the loop item, the dict entries under a non-identifier, a secret-named and a credential-shaped key, the conditional's side and the setattr value are all refused, and imports.py's clipped module path drops its middle marker."
